{
  "step_by_step_thinking": "1. Convert the QT interval from milliseconds to seconds: 217 ms = 0.217 s. 2. Calculate the RR interval from the heart rate: RR = 60 seconds / HR = 60 / 140 ≈ 0.4286 s. 3. Compute the square root of the RR interval: √RR ≈ √0.4286 ≈ 0.6547. 4. Apply Bazett's formula: QTc = QT / √RR = 0.217 s / 0.6547 ≈ 0.3315 s. 5. Convert the corrected QT back to milliseconds: 0.3315 s × 1000 ≈ 332 ms.",
  "answer": "≈332 msec"
}

{
