  "step_by_step_thinking": "The Wells criteria for DVT include: (1) Active cancer – none (0); (2) Paralysis/immobilization – none (0); (3) Recent surgery/bed rest within 4 weeks – surgery was 6 weeks ago (0); (4) Localized tenderness along deep veins – present (1); (5) Entire leg swelling – not described (0); (6) Calf swelling >3 cm compared to the other leg – difference is 1.3 cm (0); (7) Pitting edema – absent (0); (8) Collateral superficial veins – present (1); (9) Prior documented DVT – yes, opposite leg 5 years ago (1); (10) Alternative diagnosis at least as likely – examiner felt DVT most likely, so no subtraction (0). Adding the points: 1 + 1 + 1 = 3. Therefore the patient's Wells score for DVT is 3.",
